{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-15T02:44:32.648Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dec610b5c29dc08047ecfcc1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-15T02:44:32.648Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Greptile review on a5b25d0f9 (P2, verified): the direct spelling fold compared raw values with isDeepStrictEqual, so equivalent spellings of one flag conflicted: { many: [false], \"no-many\": true } on a list boolean ([false] vs false), \"true,false\" vs [true, false] on a CSV list, and (pre-existing, same seam) \"true\" vs true on a scalar boolean. isSameDirectOptionValue now compares values as normalization reads them: a CSV list splits and trims, a repeatable and a scalar are never trimmed, nullish list entries drop, and a valid typed token compares as its coerced value; a blank entry or a token that is not a valid value of the kind stays raw, so it never equals a valid value and strict refusal cannot be masked. A probe of 6 declarations x 16 values shows a value passed under two spellings, or under its canonical and inverted negated spellings, now always equals the value passed once, except the documented coerce-mode non-boolean tokens a negation cannot invert. CodeRabbit (docs/SDK.md, Minor): the read_output paragraph claimed validation before any output_format service; it now says a structured replacement is validated in place of the handler result."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-15T02:44:32.648Z"}],"before_hash":"e5dfd0fba1d6c532c52793062fde63b2d501e27476aa3ffdab7570f96c804dd3","after_hash":"fc4cba1bb41d3791f66c46e6870930933f070332ae993ad186c0be2c7c3c0463","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"ebd316ac255dbb4e0c07d4e171644e55b97cf63a4186d28828211ef6b7a51260"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-15T02:54:26.821Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"dec610b5c29dc08047ecfcc1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"note_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/notes/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-15T02:54:26.820Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 16 on 0467438c9 (P2, verified): the comparator that approximated normalization dropped a null that strict repeatable validation refuses, so { many: [true], \"--many\": [true, null] } reached the handler while either spelling alone, or the reversed order, was refused. Replaced the approximation with the native path (the session method hook: call the pipeline, do not re-implement it): deliverDirectOptionValue runs each colliding spelling's value alone through refuseDirectDeclarationViolations and the shared coercer with its recorded occurrences, and the fold compares the delivered values. Every spelling is validated before either is discarded. An order probe over 6 declarations x 23 x 23 value pairs in both orders shows zero mismatches: a pair is refused exactly when either spelling alone is refused or the two deliver different values, and an accepted pair delivers the single-spelling value. An invalid second spelling now gets the value refusal it gets alone (extension_flag_value_invalid) instead of extension_option_spelling_conflict."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-15T02:54:26.821Z"}],"before_hash":"fc4cba1bb41d3791f66c46e6870930933f070332ae993ad186c0be2c7c3c0463","after_hash":"3d77b77b6d45f42ff9ef70366d93a790e4d5b6779364b4dbc3c08c910a43ed0e","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1062813af158f3ed54fb1b7ead4780ab44bc7337595dc1e786064a7f13a3ab9a"}
